    "message": "Symbian: fix native password capacity and mask host FEP text\n\nThe native password query used 256 in both SECRETED and SetMaxLength, exceeding\nCEikSecretEditor's documented maximum of 255 and causing EIKCTL 13. Keep the\nusername limit at 256 and use the SDK secret-editor limit for the password.\nPreserve resource IDs and cover the separate native limits in the host adapter.\n\nExport EKA0029 to pass the official secret capability through a new A6 request,\nwith QLineEdit::Password selected before initial text. Keep the A0 ABI and the\nordinary multiline path. Archive target builds, ABI/proxy checks, sampled real\npassword-FEP Cancel/Submit/empty acceptance and original failed auth calibration.\n\nC21 full browser link, ARM/resource checks and native auth host contracts pass.\nThe fixed empty password query opens in the real browser. Actual Basic/Digest\ncredential matrix and official shutdown remain pending; CookieStore stays local.\nArchive verified CI0.3.43 artifacts and the seven-case C17 touch regression.",
